# CVE-2026-53615: integer overflow in libblkid (util-linux), triggered by a
# crafted disk image presented to the kernel (USB/loop-mount). This API
# service never handles block devices -- unreachable in this context.
# Debian's trixie-security fix (util-linux 2.41.5-0+deb13u1) exists but may
# not have propagated into the python:3.12-slim-trixie image yet as of
# 2026-08-20. Remove this line once it has -- check:
# https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53615
CVE-2026-53615

# CVE-2026-53614: nosuid/noexec bypass in SUID mount(8) via
# LIBMOUNT_FORCE_MOUNT2. Requires local shell access to set environment
# variables before invoking mount(8) as another user -- this container runs
# a single non-root process with no shell access exposed. Same trixie-security
# fix (util-linux 2.41.5-0+deb13u1) as above; the Dockerfile now force-upgrades
# util-linux at build time, so this should become unnecessary once confirmed.
CVE-2026-53614
